#+TITLE: Understanding 2026 LLMs

* Understanding 2026 LLM Developments

** Intro

On November 24th, 2025, Anthropic released [[https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-opus-4-5][Claude Opus 4.5]]. To many people who were not [[https://planetbanatt.net/articles/deepseek.html][plugged in]] [[https://planetbanatt.net/articles/deepseek2.html][to how LLMs]] [[https://planetbanatt.net/articles/agentic.html][have been improving]], this release came as [[https://www.reddit.com/r/ClaudeAI/comments/1pmgk5c/opus_45_is_the_first_model_that_makes_me_actually/][a big shock]]. It was the first model release where the average software engineer finally started thinking "this might write better code than me."[fn:1]

About one year later, this, too, is mundane. Current frontier language models solved [[https://openai.com/index/navier-stokes-solution/][the Navier-Stokes Millennium Prize Problem]], as well as [[https://github.com/openai/math][hundreds of other high profile unsolved math problems]]. On the [[https://artificialanalysis.ai/evaluations/artificial-analysis-intelligence-index?models=claude-opus-5-5%2Cclaude-sonnet-5-5%2Cclaude-opus-5-5-xhigh%2Cclaude-opus-5-5-high%2Cclaude-fable-5-1%2Cclaude-fable-5-1-xhigh%2Cgpt-6-astra%2Cgemini-4-argon%2Cgpt-6-astra-xhigh%2Cclaude-sonnet-5-5-xhigh%2Cgpt-6-1-sol%2Cmuse-spark-1-3%2Cgpt-6-sol%2Cgrok-4-7%2Cmimo-v2-6-pro%2Cqwen3-8-max%2Cglm-5-3%2Cstep-5%2Ckimi-k3%2Cclaude-haiku-5-5%2Cglm-5-3-flash%2Cgemini-3-8-flash%2Cdeepseek-v4-1-flash%2Cmistral-large-4%2Cgpt-6-luna%2Cqwen3-8-27b%2Ck2-horizon-375b-a23b%2Cminimax-m3%2Cinkling%2Cnvidia-nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b%2Cmuse-glimmer%2Cclaude-opus-4-5-thinking%2Cclaude-opus-4-5][Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index]], Opus 4.5 scores a 29, below models like GPT-6-Luna, DeepSeek-v4.1-Flash, even models like [[https://artificialanalysis.ai/models/qwen3-8-27b][Qwen 3.8 27B]], which can run on a single user's GPU[fn:2].

