*** GLM-5.3

GLM-5.3 was an update to the GLM-5 line which scaled up the post-training. This was a big upgrade in ability over GLM-5.2 despite using the same underlying model. However, it's one example of the shifting trend in frontier language modeling away from pretraining: the majority of compute nowadays is spent on post-training and inference, and intuitions on how these models work based on insights from pretraining may not hold up as well as they used to.

[[../images/from_clipboard/20261008_160420.png]]

Z.ai's post on GLM-5.3 can be found [[https://z.ai/blog/glm-5.3][here]]. It came out on August 14, 2026. The details are somewhat light compared to 5.2. It's just "more environments, more diverse tasks, and more compute." The big takeaway is just that: most of the gains at the frontier are found in post-training. 

