** TODO GLM-5.3-Flash

This post can be found [[https://z.ai/blog/glm-5.3-flash][here]]. It came out on August 26, 2026.

GLM-5.3-flash was a separate model architecture compared to the GLM-5 line, with the intent to make it more efficient and natively multimodal. They got a really, really good result with this. The model was anonymously tested on openrouter as "ox-alpha" free for a week, and they served 40T+ tokens with no capacity problems.

5.3-flash mostly mixes together stuff we've already seen so far. They use manifold-constrained hyper-connections, multi-token prediction, and a mix of linear and sparse attention. The model is still pretty large, at 320B parameters, but most of that is width: the model has only 45 layers and activates just 18B. In effect this means that the model is outrageously cheap to serve: it's priced at $0.03/$0.40, which is comparable to GPT-6 Luna at $0.10/$0.50[fn:7].

[[../images/from_clipboard/20261009_154559.png]]

Their big technical contribution is IndexPool, which ???

5.3-flash was also specifically trained for self-verification loops, which hints at why they made the jump to natively multimodal training. That is, they write some code for something, take a screenshot of the output, and then use that screenshot to identify things that need to be improved. Their stated results here use websites as a test case but this loop can easily be applied to any code which produces a visual artifact. 

